ref_dict.prop:generators:
\begin{proposition}\label{prop:generators}
There are unique elements $z_k\in \Omega^k(\OGr(n))$ for $1\leqslant k\leqslant n$, such that the monomials $z_1^{i_1}z_2^{i_2}\dots z_n^{i_n}$ for $i_k\in \{0,1\}$ form a free basis of $\Omega^*(\OGr(n))$ over $\mathbb{L}$, and the Chern classes of $\taut_n^\vee$ are computed as follows (where $F_\Omega(t,t)=:\sum_{i=1}^\infty d_it^i$):
$$
    c_k^\Omega(\taut_n^\vee)=(-1)^k\sum\limits_{i=0}^{n-k} d_{i+1}z_{k+i}.
$$
\end{proposition}

