Finally, in the course of proving \cref{thm:mainthm}, we find an analogue of a theorem by Goto--Nakamura in terms of $\qs$ for local rings with isolated non-CMFI loci.

\begin{Theoremx}[\Cref{thm: CMFI-pun}]\label{thm:mainthm-B}
    Let $(R,\mathfrak{m})$ be a $d$-dimensional excellent equidimensional local ring of prime characteristic $p>0$. The following are equivalent.
    \begin{enumerate}[label=(\alph*)]
        \item For all $\mathfrak{p}\in\operatorname{Spec}(R)\smallsetminus\{\mathfrak{m}\}$, the localization $R_\mathfrak{p}$ is Cohen--Macaulay and $F$-injective.
        \item $R$ is generalized Cohen--Macaulay and $\ell_R\left( 0^F_{H^d_\mathfrak{m}(R)}\right)<\infty$.
        \item $\sup\{\ell_R( \qs /\mathfrak{q})\mid \mathfrak{q} \text{ is a parameter ideal}\}<\infty$.
    \end{enumerate}
\end{Theoremx}

